course: dictionary
lesson: 5555
title: Lemurs of Madagascar
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A lemur is a furry animal with big eyes, a pointed face and usually a long tail. In the wild, lemurs live only on the island of Madagascar, off the coast of Africa. «The indri is the biggest living lemur» tells you that lemur is the name of a whole group of animals, and that there are many kinds.
explain: The sentences give you clues to what lemurs are like. «Sifakas are lemurs built for leaping between trees» tells you lemurs are good at jumping through trees. «Ring-tailed lemurs sit in the morning sun» tells you they often rest in the sun to get warm.
explain: Some words in the sentences name other animals, not lemurs. «The fossa is Madagascar's biggest meat-eater, shaped like a slim cat» tells you a fossa is a different animal, and it is related to mongooses. When you read about lemurs, check each sentence to see which animal it is describing.
fact: A lemur is a furry animal with big eyes, a pointed face and usually a long tail.
fact: In the wild, lemurs live only on the island of Madagascar, off the coast of Africa.
fact: The ring-tailed lemur is the best-known kind, with a long black-and-white striped tail.
fact: Lemurs are primates, like monkeys and apes.
fact: Many kinds of lemur are endangered, which means they are in danger of dying out, often because their forests are cut down.
exercise: «The indri is the biggest living lemur.» What is a lemur? | A bird that cannot fly | A tree that grows in deserts | A type of fish that lives in the sea | *A furry animal with big eyes and a pointed face
exercise: Where do lemurs live in the wild? | In every country in Europe | Only in zoos | *Only on the island of Madagascar | In the deserts of Asia
exercise: «Ring-tailed lemurs sit in the morning sun.» Which lemur has a long black-and-white striped tail? | *Ring-tailed lemur | Indri | Sifaka | Fossa
test:
test: Why are many lemurs endangered? | They have grown too big to move | *Their forests are being cut down | They sing too loudly | They only eat fish
test: Which group of animals are lemurs part of? | Reptiles | Birds | *Primates | Cats
exam: Lemurs are found in the wild only on which island? | *Madagascar | Sri Lanka | Cuba | Iceland
